x", -11.82493782043457]]}, {"t": " \\", "lp": -0.0017815595492720604, "top": [[" \\", -0.0017815595492720604], ["\n", -6.864531993865967]]}, {"t": "\n", "lp": -0.0005280577461235225, "top": [["\n", -0.0005280577461235225], ["\n\n", -11.668839454650879]]}, {"t": "```", "lp": -0.0004738499701488763, "top": [["```", -0.0004738499701488763], ["-", -10.188769340515137]]}, {"t": "\n", "lp": -0.0006154284928925335, "top": [["\n", -0.0006154284928925335], ["\n\n", -8.068131446838379]]}, {"t": "Use", "lp": -1.4414706230163574, "top": [["Uses", -1.1291403770446777], ["Use", -1.4414706230163574]]}, {"t": " Intel", "lp": -0.19955453276634216, "top": [[" Intel", -0.19955453276634216], [" **", -2.0360662937164307]]}, {"t": "'s", "lp": -0.0989520326256752, "top": [["'s", -0.0989520326256752], [" compilers", -2.679743528366089]]}], "text": "# PKGBUILD build() Function \u2014 Step by Step\n\nLet me break down this `build()` function line by line, explaining the purpose of each flag.\n\n## Setup Commands\n\n```bash\nsource /opt/intel/oneapi/setvars.sh --force\n```\nThis loads the Intel oneAPI environment variables (PATH, library paths, etc.) so that `icx`/`icpx` compilers are discoverable. The `--force` flag forces the environment to be set even if the script detects it's already sourced.\n\n```bash\nset -e\n```\nMakes the shell exit immediately if any command returns a non-zero status. This catches build failures early.\n\n## The CMake Configuration\n\n```bash\ncmake -S \"${srcdir}/llama.cpp\" -B \"${srcdir}/build\" -G Ninja \\\n```\n| Flag | Meaning |\n|------|---------|\n| `-S \"${srcdir}/llama.cpp\"` | **Source directory** \u2014 where the CMakeLists.txt lives |\n| `-B \"${srcdir}/build\"` | **Build directory** \u2014 out-of-source build location |\n| `-G Ninja` | **Generator** \u2014 use Ninja for fast, parallel builds |\n\n## Build Type and Installation\n\n```bash\n-DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release \\\n```\nOptimization flags enabled (`-O3`, etc.). No debug symbols.\n\n```bash\n-DCMAKE_INSTALL_PREFIX=/usr \\\n```\nWhere binaries install (standard system location).\n\n```bash\n-DCMAKE_INSTALL_LIBDIR=lib \\\n```\nForces libraries into `lib/` rather than `lib64/` (Arch standard).\n\n## Compiler Selection\n\n```bash\n-DCMAKE_C_COMPILER=icx \\\n-DCMAKE_CXX_COMPILER=icpx \\\n```\nUse Intel's"}